# The build context is the repo root, because the Dockerfile COPYs
# scripts/llm-sim.py from where it LIVES rather than from a vendored second copy
# (see the header there). That would otherwise ship the whole repo — two Helm
# value trees, Terraform state, the dashboards, .git — to the daemon on every
# build.
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit the one file the image actually needs. An
# allowlist rather than a denylist on purpose: a new top-level directory is
# excluded by default instead of silently enlarging the context.
*
!scripts/llm-sim.py
